---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
---
<Layout>
<section class="hero wrap">
<div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"/> INDEPENDENT ENGINEER · BASED IN MALTA</div><h1>Complex systems.<br/><em>Clear decisions.</em></h1><p class="intro">I build and improve backend systems — with a focus on reliability, integrations, and the trade-offs that matter in production.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#work">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="mailto:raul.almeida@arsoluciondigital.com">Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="hero-foot mono">GO / PHP / SQL <span>LESS MAGIC. MORE UNDERSTANDING.</span></div></div>
<figure class="hero-portrait"><div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/images/raul-almeida-portrait.jpg" width="400" height="400" alt="Raúl Almeida, smiling, wearing a blue jacket" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/></div><figcaption><span><strong>Raúl Almeida</strong><span>Engineer. Founder. Curious by nature.</span></span><span class="mono">MALTA / EUROPE</span></figcaption></figure>
</section>
<div class="principle-band"><div class="wrap"><span class="mono">HOW I APPROACH THE WORK</span><p>Understand the problem. <span>Make the smallest sound change.</span> Verify it.</p></div></div>
<section id="work" class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / SELECTED WORK</span><h2>Decisions, not just deliverables.</h2></div><p>A closer look at the code, the constraints,<br/>and what I chose to leave out.</p></div>
<article class="project"><div class="project-visual wallet-visual"><div class="visual-top mono"><span>TRANSACTION BOUNDARY</span><span>SQL / BACKEND</span></div><div class="transaction"><div><span class="step-number">01</span><span>Lock the account</span></div><div><span class="step-number">02</span><span>Check idempotency</span></div><div><span class="step-number">03</span><span>Apply the operation</span></div><div><span class="step-number">04</span><span>Commit together</span></div></div><p class="mono visual-caption">CORRECTNESS BEFORE CLEVERNESS.</p></div><div class="project-copy"><span class="eyebrow">BACKEND ENGINEERING · TECHNICAL ASSIGNMENT</span><h3>A wallet that takes<br/>consistency seriously.</h3><p>Deposits, withdrawals and retries turn a small API into a useful test of engineering judgement. The interesting part is what happens when requests compete.</p><div class="tags"><span>PHP</span><span>MySQL</span><span>Idempotency</span></div><details><summary>Inside the decisions <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Lock the account row within the transaction, then check the idempotency key. Keep the balance change and the operation record in the same transaction. The repository contains the implementation and its tests; this is a technical assignment, not a live banking product.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/raulalmeidatarazona/wallet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="project reverse"><div class="project-visual media-visual"><div class="visual-top mono"><span>MEDIA SIGNAL SERVICE</span><span>CONTENT → CONTEXT</span></div><div class="article-sample"><span class="mono">UNTRUSTED INPUT</span><div class="sample-line long"></div><div class="sample-line"></div><div class="sample-line short"></div></div><div class="media-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="signal-output"><span>Searchable articles</span><span>Enrichment</span><span>Trends</span></div><p class="mono visual-caption">USEFUL OUTPUT. EXPLICIT LIMITS.</p></div><div class="project-copy"><span class="eyebrow">FULL-STACK ENGINEERING · TECHNICAL ASSIGNMENT</span><h3>From news articles<br/>to useful signals.</h3><p>A small media intelligence service exploring boolean search, LLM enrichment and time-based aggregates — without treating a model response as a source of truth.</p><div class="tags"><span>NestJS</span><span>React</span><span>PostgreSQL</span></div><details><summary>Inside the decisions <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Define the API contract, separate domain rules from infrastructure, and make model cost and failure modes explicit. This assignment includes the reasoning and development transcript alongside the code.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/raulalmeidatarazona/carma-challenge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article>
</section>
<section id="notes" class="notes-section"><div class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / FIELD NOTES</span><h2>Things worth understanding.</h2></div><p>Short explanations. Concrete problems.<br/>No architecture for architecture’s sake.</p></div><div class="notes-toolbar"><p class="mono">WRITING & EXPLANATIONS</p><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter notes"><button data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All notes</button><button data-filter="backend" aria-pressed="false">Backend</button><button data-filter="ai" aria-pressed="false">AI & workflow</button></div></div><div class="notes-list"><a class="note-row" data-category="backend" href="/notes/retries-are-not-a-strategy/"><span class="mono note-index">01</span><div><span class="eyebrow">RELIABILITY / BACKEND</span><h3>Retries are not a consistency strategy.</h3><p>Before retrying a request, decide what a repeated request means.</p></div><span class="row-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="note-row" data-category="ai" href="/notes/using-ai-without-outsourcing-judgement/"><span class="mono note-index">02</span><div><span class="eyebrow">AI / ENGINEERING PRACTICE</span><h3>Use AI. Keep the judgement.</h3><p>Fast implementation is useful. Evidence is what makes it trustworthy.</p></div><span class="row-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="video-note"><span class="mono">WATCH / LEARN</span><p>Start with an existing community recording. Technical explainers and ordered video series will grow from here.</p><a class="text-link" href="#talks">Explore talks & recordings ↓</a></div></div></section>
<section id="talks" class="section wrap talks-section">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / TALKS & CONVERSATIONS</span><h2>Ideas are better<br/>when you share them.</h2></div><p>On stage and in conversation. <br/>Watch here, or go straight to the source.</p></div>
  <div class="talks-layout">
    <article class="recorded-talk">
      <VideoEmbed title="APIs y Automatización — WordCamp Cartagena 2024" thumbnail="/images/wordcamp-cartagena-talk.jpg" embedUrl="https://video.wordpress.com/embed/NCcNgffg?hd=1&autoPlay=1&permalink=1&loop=0&muted=0&playsinline=1&controls=1&cover=1" sourceUrl="https://wordpress.tv/2024/07/23/apis-y-automatizacion-transformando-tu-wordpress-en-una-maquina-de-negocios/" sourceLabel="Open on WordPress.tv" />
      <div class="recording-copy"><span class="eyebrow">WORDCAMP CARTAGENA · 8 JUNE 2024 · SPANISH</span><h3 lang="es">APIs y Automatización: Transformando tu WordPress en una Máquina de Negocios</h3><p>Connecting WooCommerce, customer relationships and warehouse operations through APIs. A practical talk about making business systems work together.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="recorded-talk festival-talk">
      <VideoEmbed title="Raúl Almeida — Sustainable Fashion Fest 2026, from 1:41:44" thumbnail="/images/sustainable-fashion-fest.jpg" embedUrl="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/T6qQIuMQZ1A?start=6104&autoplay=1&playsinline=1&rel=0" sourceUrl="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T6qQIuMQZ1A&t=6104s" sourceLabel="Open on YouTube at 1:41:44" playLabel="Play from 1:41:44" />
      <div class="recording-copy"><span class="eyebrow">SUSTAINABLE FASHION FEST 2026 · BARCELONA</span><h3>Technology meets<br/>sustainable fashion.</h3><p>My contribution to the festival’s day-three conference. Playback starts at my appearance, 1:41:44 into the original broadcast.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="community-recording">
      <VideoEmbed title="Desarrollar en WordPress con Raul Almeida" thumbnail="/images/wordpress-cartagena-video.jpg" embedUrl="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/YV-pVvkb68U?autoplay=1&playsinline=1&rel=0" sourceUrl="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YV-pVvkb68U" sourceLabel="Open on YouTube" />
      <div class="recording-copy"><span class="eyebrow">FROM THE COMMUNITY ARCHIVE · WORDPRESS CARTAGENA</span><h3 lang="es">Desarrollar en WordPress<br/>con Raul Almeida</h3><p>A conversation with the WordPress Cartagena community. Original recording in Spanish, hosted on their YouTube channel.</p></div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="about" class="section wrap about"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE CODE</span><h2>Hi, I’m Raúl.<br/><em>I like making things<br/>make sense.</em></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="large-copy">A backend engineer and systems architect, based in Malta. My work lives where software meets operational reality.</p><p>That means integrations that need to survive retries, databases under contention, and established systems that need to evolve without a rewrite.</p><p>I work with Go, PHP and SQL. Through AR Solución Digital, I also help teams understand technical problems before committing to expensive changes.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://arsoluciondigital.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About AR Solución Digital ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="contact-section"><div class="wrap contact"><div><span class="eyebrow">HAVE A SYSTEM WORTH THINKING ABOUT?</span><h2>Let’s start with<br/><em>the real problem.</em></h2></div><div><p>Engineering roles, thoughtful collaborations,<br/>or a difficult backend problem.</p><a class="button light" href="mailto:raul.almeida@arsoluciondigital.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:raul.almeida@arsoluciondigital.com">raul.almeida@arsoluciondigital.com</a></div></div></section>
<div class="preview-bar mono">DESIGN PREVIEW · FIRST EDITION · COPY OPEN FOR REVIEW</div>
<script>
const filters = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]');
filters.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
 filters.forEach(item => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-category]').forEach(note => { note.hidden = button.dataset.filter !== 'all' && note.dataset.category !== button.dataset.filter; });
}));
</script>
</Layout>
